# Test: commit-revisions caps the files a file:// archive location keeps
# VALIDATES: with `commit-revisions 2` and a file:// archive block, three
#   `ze config archive local` runs against a live daemon leave exactly the two
#   newest archive files, oldest pruned first, and a .conf file no archive block
#   wrote stays in place.
# PREVENTS: the cap being parsed but never applied, so an archive directory grows
#   without bound on a router that archives on every change.
#
# The fixture (internal/test/fixture/config_archive_prune_fixture.go) starts the
# daemon itself, because the archive location must be an absolute path private
# to this run and the CLI needs the daemon's SSH credentials. It returns an
# error, reported through ZE-OBSERVER-FAIL, when any round's file set differs
# from the newest two.
option=timeout:value=60s

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=le test fixture ui/config-archive-prune
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=OK: commit-revisions 2 kept
